15 0 obj
<< /A 37 0 R /Alt (Seven-panel box plot chart compares blood parameters among untreated \(UT\), 10 mGy, and 100 mGy groups. Panels show WBC \(A\), RBC \(B\), HGB \(C\), PLT \(D\), percent lymphocytes \(E\), percent monocytes \(F\), and percent neutrophil \(G\). Color-coded boxes represent each group with black data points. Panel G highlights statistical differences using asterisk and \215ns\216 labels.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 28 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
16 0 obj
<< /A 38 0 R /Alt (Figure composed of multiple grouped box plots showing cell type percentages under three conditions: untreated \(UT, red\), 10 milligray \(green\), and 100 milligray \(blue\). Panel A presents five plots for T cells, NK cells, myeloid cells, dendritic cells, and B cells, showing similar distributions except B cells with a significant decrease at 100 milligray. Panel B displays four plots for TCRb- CD3-, TCRb+ CD3-, TCRb- CD3+, and TCRb+ CD3+ cells, plus subplots for DN, DP, CD4 SP, and CD8 SP cell populations, illustrating slight shifts between treatments. Panel C includes T cells, NK cells, and myeloid and granulocyte plots by marker expression, each with separate condition distributions.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 29 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
17 0 obj
<< /A 39 0 R /Alt <> /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 30 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
18 0 obj
<< /A 40 0 R /Alt (Panel A shows a principal component analysis plot with three sample groups distinguished by color; panel B displays two volcano plots of differential gene expression comparing UT versus 100mGy and UT versus 10mGy; panel C is a heatmap illustrating gene expression across three conditions; panel D presents a Venn diagram comparing upregulated and downregulated genes between dose treatments; panel E contains four line charts of Z-scores for selected gene clusters across UT, 10mGy, and 100mGy; panel F shows six scatter plots indicating transcript abundance \(TPM\) for specific genes in each treatment group.) /K 0 /P 8 0 R /Pg 31 0 R /S /Figure /T () >>
endobj
